WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.070
We are back, and having the exact conversation

2
00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.680
that I fantasized about.

3
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.180
Something that is very honest, very deep, very candid,

4
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.200
humor, breaking it all down.

5
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.900
Thank you for doing this with me.

6
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.850
Okay, there's a quote that I love.

7
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.980
It said, "Trust patterns; not apologies."

8
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:18.813
Wow.

9
00:00:18.813 --> 00:00:20.100
I know.

10
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.510
Brilliant. True.
Right?

11
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.343
Yeah.

12
00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.470
Trust patterns, not apologies.

13
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.110
Do you think he'll ever change?

14
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.130
That's a big part of this process.

15
00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.460
This disclosure process that couples go through.

16
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.211
And, you know, some people get to the end of the process

17
00:00:33.211 --> 00:00:35.760 line:15%
and it's where you have to share the full truth

18
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.090 line:15%
and process it together.

19
00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.750 line:15%
And some couples choose to stay together.

20
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.680 line:15%
It did not end up being the right decision for us.

21
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.490
And in the end, what is the most important thing

22
00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.840
to both of us, our child.

23
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.570
I mean, it is all about him.

24
00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.280
You know, when Anthony, you know, Anthony was sentenced

25
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.240
to federal prison for a little under two years

26
00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.710
and my son was five.

27
00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:57.400
And I said, I am not under any circumstances

28
00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.870
gonna take him to visit his father.

29
00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.020
Like I would not put him...

30
00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.570
It will be too traumatic.

31
00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.870
And I remember we went away for the holidays

32
00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:04.703
and we traveled.

33
00:01:04.703 --> 00:01:06.400
We were lucky enough to travel with the Clintons.

34
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.370
And here we are, we're at this beautiful house,

35
00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:10.770
this beautiful resort, and we're going out

36
00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.840
to dinner every night

37
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.850
and the kids are playing in the beach and playing.

38
00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:14.920
You know, I mean,

39
00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:16.860
it is essentially heaven.
Fantasy.

40
00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:17.770
Right? Fantasy.

41
00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:19.830
And one night we're at dinner with this family

42
00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.110
we had just met on the beach,

43
00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:23.080
and the little boy who was my son's age

44
00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.760
goes up to his father and puts his hands up in the air

45
00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:26.900
to be lifted.

46
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.180
And the man, the father lifts up the son, Joseph,

47
00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.720
and is holding him.

48
00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:35.100
And Jordan turns to me and just breaks down and says,

49
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.420
I want my daddy, I want my daddy.

50
00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.070
And was inconsolable.

51
00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:43.070
And that was my, like, that was my moment of

52
00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.910
you can give everything to your child

53
00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:48.000
if you have the capacity to

54
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.610
that is tangible, that is things,

55
00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.000
but nothing is gonna replace the hole in the heart

56
00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.360
that is the absence of a parent.

57
00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.760
And I made a promise to him.

58
00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.160
The next day I said, I would take him to see his dad.

59
00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.090
And I did.

60
00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:05.870
I appreciate that high road behavior so much.

61
00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.060
So here you are.

62
00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:10.930
I sure am.

63
00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.500
In the analogy and metaphors of books,

64
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.560
what is your next chapter?

65
00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:18.340
Every day I wake up and I'm healthy and happy

66
00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.226
and have my little boy.

67
00:02:19.226 --> 00:02:22.600 line:15%
I am grateful, I have gratitude for that

68
00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.650 line:15%
because I've also had an extraordinarily privileged life.

69
00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.258
I've been walked in spaces and places,

70
00:02:28.258 --> 00:02:30.480
you know, that I would have never imagined.

71
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.500
And so I do have the ability to get up and say,

72
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:33.550
you know what?

73
00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:37.090
I'm opening up my life, my truth,

74
00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.387
and it's been pretty amazing.

75
00:02:39.387 --> 00:02:40.810
And I wanna hear that from people

76
00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.460
who have walked through the fire.

77
00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.290
Okay, last question, woman to woman.

78
00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.010
Did you ever tell Anthony,

79
00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:50.436
I love you, but I'm not taking your last name.

80
00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.860
(Huma laughs)

81
00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.210
It wasn't...

82
00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:55.171
It never even came up.

83
00:02:55.171 --> 00:02:57.440
It was not even an issue

84
00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.410
that I was gonna take his last name.

85
00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.950
In fact, at one point, yeah, he didn't even ask.

86
00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.400
It's so funny.

87
00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.600
Okay, you're here this moment.

88
00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.830
I can't wait to see what unveils next.

89
00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:11.003
I thank you.

90
00:03:11.003 --> 00:03:14.319
(audience applauding)

91
00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:15.152
Thank you so much for this profound conversation

92
00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:20.310
that I've been waiting to have for so many weeks.

93
00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:23.170
Since this book came out, everybody's talking about it.

94
00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:26.877
Huma Abedin, her New York Times best selling memoir,

95
00:03:26.877 --> 00:03:31.300
"Both/And: A Life in Many Worlds" is on sale right now.

96
00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.740
Thank you, Huma.

97
00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:33.573
Thank you.

98
00:03:33.573 --> 00:03:37.201
We'll be right back.

99
00:03:37.201 --> 00:03:39.784 line:15%
